 r←Test_TableEdit_023(stopFlag batchFlag);parms;n;⎕TRAP;table;rowTitles
⍝ Ctrl+X and Ctrl+V on a block of cells in "Scroll" mode.
 r←T._Inactive
 :Return

 r←T._Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 table←⍉⊃('Obama' 'Bush' 'Clinton' 'Reagan' 'Kennedy' 'Carter')(1 0 1 0 1 1)
 table←table,table
 parms←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Table.CreateParms
 parms.posn←35 25
 parms.size←400 600
 parms.colTitles←'Name' 'Democrat'
 parms.addToCaption←'Testing Table.Run'
 parms.confirmQuit←0
 parms.testMode←1
 parms.dataTypes←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Enums.TableDataTypes.(Character Numeric Character YesNo)

 n←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Table.Create table #.APLGUI.APLGUI.APLGuiGlobalParms.CreateDefaults parms

 n.Grid.CurCell←1 0
 n.Grid.SelItems←(1 0)(2 1)
 n.Grid ∆KeyPress⊂'CT'    ⍝TODO⍝  This causes a GridCopyError - why?!
 ∆Process n.∆Form
 n.Grid.CurCell←2 2
 n.Grid.SelItems←(2 3)(3 4)
 n.Grid ∆KeyPress⊂'PT'
 ∆Process n.∆Form
 table[1 2;0 1]←2 2⍴'' 0
 table[2 3;2 3]←2 2⍴'Bush' 0 'Clinton' 1
 →T.GoToTidyUp n.Grid.Values≢table

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 n.∆CloseForm
